{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/92814-could-you-look-over-my-game","id":92814,"title":"Could you look over my game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-17T08:46:12-07:00","id":92814,"title":"Could you look over my game?","content":"I dabble in making new role-playing games. I bet many of us have, either borrowing mechanics from another game or made something up by ourselves. I'm currently dabbling in three, two of which have gotten fairly far in the developing stages. One game I'm working on has reached a point where I think it is ready to be play-tested by my peers. I've written it down and now I just need some idio... I mean, willing participants, to read over the file and see if they can find any obvious contradictions or errors. If all is good, I intend to release the game into public play-testing and hopefully I can release the game for sale one day (currently shooting for next year).<br /> <br /> Anyway, before you jump to the occasion, a word of warning: The file is close to 80 pages, not counting the table of content or the cover page. I do not expect you to read it all in one sitting. If you are interested at taking a look, I also expect you to give feedback, the sooner the better, even if it's as short as &quot;no errors found&quot;, just so that I know you've read through it. If you can't find anything during first reading, that's good enough for me. I expect detailed feedback during the actual play-testing. If you are still interested, send me a PM.<br /> <br /> Finally, some introduction to the actual game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The war is over, but I have to wonder if the price was worth paying. Monsters now roam freely in the night and we have abandoned the rural areas. The cities remain safe, for the most part, but not uncorrupted. We are respected but we are no longer loved. We are feared. Even while I write this, the Heretics gain more following. How they manage to deceive the people sickens me, although I can see their appeal when we have failed them. Oh, we have failed them. While the people are assaulted by monsters and daemons and wicked fairies, the Illuminated sit in our chapels and fatten ourselves to grotesque extremes. The Cardinals would condemn me for heresy should they read this, but the word must out to my fellow Saints: We have failed the people. We must correct our ways.</i> <div align=\"right\">-Eliza Wilthrow, Saint of the Illuminated Order\u200b</div> <br /> Less than twenty years ago, a religious war ended that had been fought for nearly 300 years, ever since the Last King took Illuminated Faith as his own and condemned the Nocturnal Faith. Since then, the Illuminated Order has grown in power and now controls most of the principalities of the Civilized World. The Illuminated Order won the war, but at great cost. They had to kill a god, and left the night defenceless. They drove the Nocturnals into hiding, but they are not dead, not all of them.<br /> <br /> The Nocturnals are regaining their strengths, preparing for the war to start again. Or they are hiding, hoping to live out the rest of their lives in relative peace. But they have power, power granted to them by their dead god. This makes them heretics by their very existence, as the Illuminated Order will not rest unless all that remains of the dead god has been utterly removed from the world of mortal men.<br /> <br /> Nocturnals were the champions of the night. Protectors, if you will. But the war disrupted their responsibility and has left the night all but defenceless. Monsters that used to stay in the shadows now roam freely, and the Saints of the Illuminated do nothing but keep these monsters away from the cities.<br /> <br /> Nocturnal Heresy is a game about defeat, revenge, rebellion and corrupting power. It is a game where the Players take on the roles of powerful individuals in a weak and corrupted world, who are hunted for their heresy, and who must decide how they will live out the rest of their lives. Will they hide in the shadows and try to live peacefully or on the run? Or will they rise up against those who murdered their god and bring unto them the same pain and grief? The Nocturnals have the dark power and no master to serve; it is their choice. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:22:31-07:00","id":93002,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting. I'd be interested in looking at it (I read the above, plus what you have on your link at Emerald Samurai...).<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T17:24:45-07:00","id":93087,"title":"","content":"Sounds a bit like Priest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T01:10:47-07:00","id":93300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/92814-could-you-look-over-my-game?p=93087#post93087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds a bit like Priest.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be right but the likeness would be coincidental. I've seen the film with Paul Bettany but I understand it was based on a comic that I haven't read. Maybe you're referring to something else though, but I don't think I've seen/read it. Anything you'd recommend?<br /> <br /> The game is called Nocturnal Heresy (at least currently) and focuses on the Players taking on the parts of the Nocturnals. The Saints and the Illuminated Order serve as antagonists, in a way. It focuses a bit on the conflict between the two and how neither side is good nor evil (or rather, that both sides can be equally corrupted).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T01:23:01-07:00","id":93305,"title":"","content":"I think it would be better if the game wouldn't decide for the players which side they are. Instead it should provide options and suggestion to go either way or stay in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T01:47:57-07:00","id":93313,"title":"","content":"You are absolutely right. It is not possible to portray both sides as neither good nor evil if one side is set up to be the antagonist/villain.<br /> <br /> The core will focus on the Nocturnals but I do have plans to add Saints in as a playable template as well later on. Other templates will also come in later and there is no reason for me to focus solely on the Nocturnals or the Saints. The Nocturnals are, mechanically speaking, a template to be added to the base mortal character, so you can also play a standard mortal character if that strikes your fancy.<br /> <br /> I enjoy the diversity of what sort of characters you can play, but I am going to sort of follow the White Wolf module for Exalted on this: Start with one type of character and add others down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:01:00-07:00","id":93586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/92814-could-you-look-over-my-game?p=93313#post93313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy the diversity of what sort of characters you can play, but I am going to sort of follow the White Wolf module for Exalted on this: Start with one type of character and add others down the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, its probably easier to produce in segments, just make sure your future additions won't be so 'cool' (read OP) that they totally overshadow the first options provided.<br /> A lot of RPG's have fallen into that trap causing the overall game line to suffer from ever increasing power creep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:20:49-07:00","id":93690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/92814-could-you-look-over-my-game?p=93586#post93586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, its probably easier to produce in segments, just make sure your future additions won't be so 'cool' (read OP) that they totally overshadow the first options provided.<br /> A lot of RPG's have fallen into that trap causing the overall game line to suffer from ever increasing power creep.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very good advice and I will be sure to keep it in mind. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and mor